  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Men Engage Africa 2019-2025 - Men Engage Africa Strategic Plan (New Strategy 2022-2026)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Men Engage Afrika 2019-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall goal
Scaling up gender transformative approached in advocacy, accountability culture and partnership effectiveness to advance MEA regional impact and sustainability. The Strategic Plan 20142027 has three strategic areas and in total seven objectives:

Strategic area 1: Advocacy

Objective 1: Position MEA as a leading male engagement movement in the region within its thematic areas by mobilising collective voices and actions to influence policies and legal reforms.

Objective 2: Scale up gender transformative advocacy through capacity strengthening MEA&apos;s network and strategic partners to advance feminist approaches and principles.

Strategic area 2: Accountability

Objective 3: Improve systems and structures to operationalize and popularise existing MEA accountability mechanism for effective collaboration responsiveness and functionality of the movement.

Objective 4: Advance MEA&apos;s joint actions an initiatives through capacity strengthening of partners utilising country and regional channels to achieve MEA&apos;s goals

Strategic area 3: Partnerships

Objective 5: Implement capacity strengthening initiatives on gender transformative approached including MenEngage Africa Training Initiative (MATI)

Objective 6: Identify strengthen and maintain strategic partnerships for collaboration across MEA thematic areas at national, regional and global levels.

Objective 7: Contribute to resource mobilization for the sustainability of the MEA network</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Men Engage Africa &#xE4;r ett av globala Men Engage Alliansens regionala n&#xE4;tverk. Men Engage Africa n&#xE4;tverket best&#xE5;r av 22 nationella Men Engage Africa n&#xE4;tverk (Botswana, Burundi, Kamerun, Etiopien, Demokratiska Republiken Kongo, Kenya, Lesotho, Liberia, Madagascar, Malawi, Mali, Mozambique, Namibia, Nigeria, Rwanda, Sierra Leone, Tanzania, Togo, Uganda, Zambia, Zimbabwe, Eswatini) med medlemmar p&#xE5; nationell niv&#xE5;. Men Engage n&#xE4;tverket fokuserar hur maskulinitetsnormer &#xE4;r formade, hur de p&#xE5;verkar samh&#xE4;llet, relationer och individer. K&#xE4;rnan i n&#xE4;tverkets arbete &#xE4;r att bidra till j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhet mellan k&#xF6;nen, f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xE4;lsa och r&#xE4;ttigheter (SRHR), och minska f&#xF6;rekomsten av k&#xF6;nsbaserat v&#xE5;ld genom att engagera pojkar och m&#xE4;n genom &quot;gender transformation&quot; - metoder som utmanar och f&#xF6;r&#xE4;ndrar negativa manlighetsnormer. N&#xE4;tverket har etablerat sig som en ledande akt&#xF6;r p&#xE5; global, regional och nationell niv&#xE5; inom detta f&#xE4;lt sedan 2009.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution is a project support to Sonke Gender Justice for the implementation of Men Engage Africa&apos;s Strategic Plan 2019-2024. The core of Men Engage Africa&apos;s work is qualitative work on men and masculinity within women&#x2019;s rights, SRHR and gender justice for all with the aim to contributing to Gender Equality.</narrative>
  </description>
